  "summary": "This savory <b>Italian braised beef</b> brings rich dinner flavors to your table without spending all day in the kitchen. Traditional long-simmered dishes often require several hours of patience, but this weeknight interpretation relies on thinly cut beef chuck and concentrated tomato paste to build deep flavor quickly. Sweet onions, crushed garlic, and aromatic rosemary soften in rich olive oil before bright red San Marzano tomatoes create a glossy sauce. Served over creamy polenta or warm rustic bread, this warm meal brings authentic Mediterranean warmth to any busy evening. The addition of red wine helps tenderize the meat while releasing complex aromas throughout your kitchen. A final sprinkle of fresh parsley adds brightness to balance the savory stewed beef. This recipe proves that comforting braises are not reserved exclusively for slow weekends. Your family will adore the luscious gravy and melt-in-your-mouth tenderness achieved in under an hour. Enjoy this fragrant, hearty feast alongside a crisp green salad for a complete Italian dining experience.",
